
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── Module ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Receipt Literacy                                                                                                                                            │
│ Level: beginner  |  Time: ~10-15 min                                                                                                                        │
│ Produces: txid, report                                                                                                                                      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Every blockchain interaction ends the same way: you check the receipt.                                                                                         

In this module you send a real payment on the XRPL Testnet and learn to read every field in the response — who sent what, to whom, for how much, what it cost, 
and whether it actually worked.                                                                                                                                

Press Enter to continue...Ensure your wallet is ready                                                                                                                                    

First we need a funded wallet. If you already have one from XRPL Camp or a previous session, it will be loaded automatically.                                  


  → ensure_wallet...
  Wallet loaded: rhuALqeW2TjPJQ32TFRibP2FSeHnVt43jz

Press Enter to continue...Fund your wallet                                                                                                                                               

Your wallet needs XRP to pay for transactions. We will request test XRP from the faucet — this is free and only works on the testnet.                          


  → ensure_funded...
  Requesting funds from testnet faucet...
  Funded! Balance: 100.000000 XRP

Press Enter to continue...Send a payment                                                                                                                                                 

Now send a small payment. We will attach a memo so you can find this transaction later. The memo format is: XRPLLAB|L1|<timestamp>                             

This payment goes to a fresh practice address the lab makes for this run: XRPL rejects an XRP payment to yourself (temREDUNDANT), and a payment of at least the
1 XRP base reserve to a new address creates that account. On a real network you would send to someone else.                                                    


  → submit_payment...
  XRPL rejects a payment to yourself (temREDUNDANT), so practice payments go to a fresh address made for this run:
  rLXQmvNPH5AWoDwrHgbcYKrnQvNZmbyrxK (your first payment to it creates the account)
  Payment submitted!
  TXID: 5368EF0073FDDE4BD60945E569662B959A5A1078A87B4F1AA437159BDF8F5083
  Result: tesSUCCESS
  Fee: 12 drops

Press Enter to continue...Verify the receipt                                                                                                                                             

Now let's look up your transaction on the ledger and verify every field.                                                                                       

A proper receipt check covers:                                                                                                                                 

 • Result code: tesSUCCESS means the ledger accepted it                                                                                                        
 • Amount: matches what you sent                                                                                                                               
 • Destination: matches where you sent it                                                                                                                      
 • Fee: the network fee in drops (1 XRP = 1,000,000 drops)                                                                                                     
 • Ledger index: which ledger version recorded your tx                                                                                                         
 • Validated: whether the consensus process has confirmed it                                                                                                   


  → verify_tx...
  ✓ Result: tesSUCCESS
  ✓ Fee: 12 drops
  ✓ Ledger index: 99999999
  ✓ Validated: yes

Press Enter to continue...What you proved                                                                                                                                                

You just completed the fundamental workflow of any blockchain interaction:                                                                                     

 1 You had a funded wallet (identity + resources)                                                                                                              
 2 You submitted a transaction (intent → ledger)                                                                                                               
 3 You verified the receipt (ledger → proof)                                                                                                                   

This is the skill that everything else builds on. Trust lines, DEX offers, escrows, multi-sig — they all start with "send, receive, verify."                   

Your report is saved. Run xrpl-lab proof-pack when you're ready to export your work.                                                                           


